# Cursor rules

See [.agents/AGENTS.md](file:///.agents/AGENTS.md) for all architectural invariants, Goose language conventions, and testing requirements.

## Key rules

- Read and follow [.agents/AGENTS.md](file:///.agents/AGENTS.md).
- Target language is Goose (`.goose`). Use Goose §7.10 extern syntax: `extern fn name(...) = "sym";`.
- Do not use dynamic heap allocations on wire parsing or serialization paths; use bounded arrays (`u8[..N]`) and slices (`u8[:]`).
- Run `python tools/test_runner.py --check-only` (or `just check`) before finishing changes.
- Use Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `perf:`, `style:`, `test:`, `chore:`). Do not edit `version.txt` manually.
